#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:1
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:149
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trace2 API"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:6
msgid ""
"The Trace2 API can be used to print debug, performance, and telemetry "
"information to stderr or a file.  The Trace2 feature is inactive unless "
"explicitly enabled by enabling one or more Trace2 Targets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:11
msgid ""
"The Trace2 API is intended to replace the existing (Trace1)  "
"`printf()`-style tracing provided by the existing `GIT_TRACE` and "
"`GIT_TRACE_PERFORMANCE` facilities.  During initial implementation, Trace2 "
"and Trace1 may operate in parallel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:14
msgid ""
"The Trace2 API defines a set of high-level messages with known fields, such "
"as (`start`: `argv`) and (`exit`: {`exit-code`, `elapsed-time`})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:20
msgid ""
"Trace2 instrumentation throughout the Git code base sends Trace2 messages to "
"the enabled Trace2 Targets.  Targets transform these messages content into "
"purpose-specific formats and write events to their data streams.  In this "
"manner, the Trace2 API can drive many different types of analysis."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:24
msgid ""
"Targets are defined using a VTable allowing easy extension to other formats "
"in the future.  This might be used to define a binary format, for example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:29
msgid ""
"Trace2 is controlled using `trace2.*` config values in the system and global "
"config files and `GIT_TRACE2*` environment variables.  Trace2 does not read "
"from repo local or worktree config files, nor does it respect `-c` command "
"line config settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trace2 Targets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:34
msgid ""
"Trace2 defines the following set of Trace2 Targets.  Format details are "
"given in a later section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Normal Format Target"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:41
msgid ""
"The normal format target is a traditional `printf()` format and similar to "
"the `GIT_TRACE` format.  This format is enabled with the `GIT_TRACE2` "
"environment variable or the `trace2.normalTarget` system or global config "
"setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:43
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:78
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:112
msgid "For example"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ export GIT_TRACE2=~/log.normal\n"
"$ git version\n"
"git version 2.20.1.155.g426c96fcdb\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:51
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:86
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:120
msgid "or"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git config --global trace2.normalTarget ~/log.normal\n"
"$ git version\n"
"git version 2.20.1.155.g426c96fcdb\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:59
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:94
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:128
msgid "yields"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:67
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cat ~/log.normal\n"
"12:28:42.620009 common-main.c:38                  version "
"2.20.1.155.g426c96fcdb\n"
"12:28:42.620989 common-main.c:39                  start git version\n"
"12:28:42.621101 git.c:432                         cmd_name version "
"(version)\n"
"12:28:42.621215 git.c:662                         exit elapsed:0.001227 "
"code:0\n"
"12:28:42.621250 trace2/tr2_tgt_normal.c:124       atexit elapsed:0.001265 "
"code:0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Performance Format Target"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:76
msgid ""
"The performance format target (PERF) is a column-based format to replace "
"`GIT_TRACE_PERFORMANCE` and is suitable for development and testing, "
"possibly to complement tools like `gprof`.  This format is enabled with the "
"`GIT_TRACE2_PERF` environment variable or the `trace2.perfTarget` system or "
"global config setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:83
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ export GIT_TRACE2_PERF=~/log.perf\n"
"$ git version\n"
"git version 2.20.1.155.g426c96fcdb\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:91
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git config --global trace2.perfTarget ~/log.perf\n"
"$ git version\n"
"git version 2.20.1.155.g426c96fcdb\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cat ~/log.perf\n"
"12:28:42.620675 common-main.c:38                  | d0 | main                     "
"| version      |     |           |           |            | "
"2.20.1.155.g426c96fcdb\n"
"12:28:42.621001 common-main.c:39                  | d0 | main                     "
"| start        |     |  0.001173 |           |            | git version\n"
"12:28:42.621111 git.c:432                         | d0 | main                     "
"| cmd_name     |     |           |           |            | version "
"(version)\n"
"12:28:42.621225 git.c:662                         | d0 | main                     "
"| exit         |     |  0.001227 |           |            | code:0\n"
"12:28:42.621259 trace2/tr2_tgt_perf.c:211         | d0 | main                     "
"| atexit       |     |  0.001265 |           |            | code:0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Event Format Target"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:110
msgid ""
"The event format target is a JSON-based format of event data suitable for "
"telemetry analysis.  This format is enabled with the `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` "
"environment variable or the `trace2.eventTarget` system or global config "
"setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:117
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ export GIT_TRACE2_EVENT=~/log.event\n"
"$ git version\n"
"git version 2.20.1.155.g426c96fcdb\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git config --global trace2.eventTarget ~/log.event\n"
"$ git version\n"
"git version 2.20.1.155.g426c96fcdb\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:136
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cat ~/log.event\n"
"{\"event\":\"version\",\"sid\":\"20190408T191610.507018Z-H9b68c35f-P000059a8\",\"thread\":\"main\",\"time\":\"2019-01-16T17:28:42.620713Z\",\"file\":\"common-main.c\",\"line\":38,\"evt\":\"4\",\"exe\":\"2.20.1.155.g426c96fcdb\"}\n"
"{\"event\":\"start\",\"sid\":\"20190408T191610.507018Z-H9b68c35f-P000059a8\",\"thread\":\"main\",\"time\":\"2019-01-16T17:28:42.621027Z\",\"file\":\"common-main.c\",\"line\":39,\"t_abs\":0.001173,\"argv\":[\"git\",\"version\"]}\n"
"{\"event\":\"cmd_name\",\"sid\":\"20190408T191610.507018Z-H9b68c35f-P000059a8\",\"thread\":\"main\",\"time\":\"2019-01-16T17:28:42.621122Z\",\"file\":\"git.c\",\"line\":432,\"name\":\"version\",\"hierarchy\":\"version\"}\n"
"{\"event\":\"exit\",\"sid\":\"20190408T191610.507018Z-H9b68c35f-P000059a8\",\"thread\":\"main\",\"time\":\"2019-01-16T17:28:42.621236Z\",\"file\":\"git.c\",\"line\":662,\"t_abs\":0.001227,\"code\":0}\n"
"{\"event\":\"atexit\",\"sid\":\"20190408T191610.507018Z-H9b68c35f-P000059a8\",\"thread\":\"main\",\"time\":\"2019-01-16T17:28:42.621268Z\",\"file\":\"trace2/tr2_tgt_event.c\",\"line\":163,\"t_abs\":0.001265,\"code\":0}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:138
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enabling a Target"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:142
msgid ""
"To enable a target, set the corresponding environment variable or system or "
"global config value to one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:148
msgid ""
"When trace files are written to a target directory, they will be named "
"according to the last component of the SID (optionally followed by a counter "
"to avoid filename collisions)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:154
msgid ""
"The Trace2 public API is defined and documented in `trace2.h`; refer to it "
"for more information.  All public functions and macros are prefixed with "
"`trace2_` and are implemented in `trace2.c`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:156
msgid "There are no public Trace2 data structures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:161
msgid ""
"The Trace2 code also defines a set of private functions and data types in "
"the `trace2/` directory.  These symbols are prefixed with `tr2_` and should "
"only be used by functions in `trace2.c` (or other private source files in "
"`trace2/`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:162
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conventions for Public Functions and Macros"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:166
msgid ""
"Some functions have a `_fl()` suffix to indicate that they take `file` and "
"`line-number` arguments."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:169
msgid ""
"Some functions have a `_va_fl()` suffix to indicate that they also take a "
"`va_list` argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:172
msgid ""
"Some functions have a `_printf_fl()` suffix to indicate that they also take "
"a `printf()` style format with a variable number of arguments."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:174
msgid "CPP wrapper macros are defined to hide most of these details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:175
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trace2 Target Formats"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:177
#, no-wrap
msgid "NORMAL Format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:180
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:205
msgid "Events are written as lines of the form:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "[<time> SP <filename>:<line> SP+] <event-name> [[SP] <event-message>] LF\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:185
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:230
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<event-name>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:188
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:232
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:303
msgid "is the event name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<event-message>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:191
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:257
msgid "is a free-form `printf()` message intended for human consumption."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:194
msgid ""
"Note that this may contain embedded LF or CRLF characters that are not "
"escaped, so the event may spill across multiple lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:197
msgid ""
"If `GIT_TRACE2_BRIEF` or `trace2.normalBrief` is true, the `time`, "
"`filename`, and `line` fields are omitted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:201
msgid ""
"This target is intended to be more of a summary (like GIT_TRACE) and less "
"detailed than the other targets.  It ignores thread, region, and data "
"messages, for example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "PERF Format"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:217
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[<time> SP <filename>:<line> SP+\n"
"    BAR SP] d<depth> SP\n"
"    BAR SP <thread-name> SP+\n"
"    BAR SP <event-name> SP+\n"
"    BAR SP [r<repo-id>] SP+\n"
"    BAR SP [<t_abs>] SP+\n"
"    BAR SP [<t_rel>] SP+\n"
"    BAR SP [<category>] SP+\n"
"    BAR SP DOTS* <perf-event-message>\n"
"    LF\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:219
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<depth>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:224
msgid ""
"is the git process depth.  This is the number of parent git processes.  A "
"top-level git command has depth value \"d0\".  A child of it has depth value "
"\"d1\".  A second level child has depth value \"d2\" and so on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:225
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<thread-name>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:229
msgid ""
"is a unique name for the thread.  The primary thread is called \"main\".  "
"Other thread names are of the form \"th%d:%s\" and include a unique number "
"and the name of the thread-proc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<repo-id>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:238
msgid ""
"when present, is a number indicating the repository in use.  A `def_repo` "
"event is emitted when a repository is opened.  This defines the repo-id and "
"associated worktree.  Subsequent repo-specific events will reference this "
"repo-id."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:241
msgid ""
"Currently, this is always \"r1\" for the main repository.  This field is in "
"anticipation of in-proc submodules in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:242
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<t_abs>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:245
msgid "when present, is the absolute time in seconds since the program started."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:246
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<t_rel>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:250
msgid ""
"when present, is time in seconds relative to the start of the current "
"region.  For a thread-exit event, it is the elapsed time of the thread."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:251
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<category>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:254
msgid ""
"is present on region and data events and is used to indicate a broad "
"category, such as \"index\" or \"status\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:255
#, no-wrap
msgid "`<perf-event-message>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:261
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"15:33:33.532712 wt-status.c:2310                  | d0 | main                     "
"| region_enter | r1  |  0.126064 |           | status     | label:print\n"
"15:33:33.532712 wt-status.c:2331                  | d0 | main                     "
"| region_leave | r1  |  0.127568 |  0.001504 | status     | label:print\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:265
msgid ""
"If `GIT_TRACE2_PERF_BRIEF` or `trace2.perfBrief` is true, the `time`, "
"`file`, and `line` fields are omitted."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:268
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"d0 | main                     | region_leave | r1  |  0.011717 |  0.009122 | "
"index      | label:preload\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:272
msgid ""
"The PERF target is intended for interactive performance analysis during "
"development and is quite noisy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:273
#, no-wrap
msgid "EVENT Format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:277
msgid ""
"Each event is a JSON-object containing multiple key/value pairs written as a "
"single line and followed by a LF."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:280
#, no-wrap
msgid "'{' <key> ':' <value> [',' <key> ':' <value>]* '}' LF\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:284
msgid "Some key/value pairs are common to all events and some are event-specific."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:285
#, no-wrap
msgid "Common Key/Value Pairs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:288
msgid "The following key/value pairs are common to all events:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:299
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"version\",\n"
"\t\"sid\":\"20190408T191827.272759Z-H9b68c35f-P00003510\",\n"
"\t\"thread\":\"main\",\n"
"\t\"time\":\"2019-04-08T19:18:27.282761Z\",\n"
"\t\"file\":\"common-main.c\",\n"
"\t\"line\":42,\n"
"\t...\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:301
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"event\":<event>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:304
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"sid\":<sid>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:312
msgid ""
"is the session-id.  This is a unique string to identify the process instance "
"to allow all events emitted by a process to be identified.  A session-id is "
"used instead of a PID because PIDs are recycled by the OS.  For child git "
"processes, the session-id is prepended with the session-id of the parent git "
"process to allow parent-child relationships to be identified during "
"post-processing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:313
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"thread\":<thread>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:315
msgid "is the thread name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:316
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"time\":<time>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:318
msgid "is the UTC time of the event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:319
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"file\":<filename>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:321
msgid "is source file generating the event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:322
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"line\":<line-number>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:324
msgid "is the integer source line number generating the event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:325
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"repo\":<repo-id>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:327
msgid "when present, is the integer repo-id as described previously."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:331
msgid ""
"If `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT_BRIEF` or `trace2.eventBrief` is true, the `file` and "
"`line` fields are omitted from all events and the `time` field is only "
"present on the \"start\" and \"atexit\" events."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:332
#, no-wrap
msgid "Event-Specific Key/Value Pairs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:334
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"version\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:342
msgid ""
"This event gives the version of the executable and the EVENT format. It "
"should always be the first event in a trace session. The EVENT format "
"version will be incremented if new event types are added, if existing fields "
"are removed, or if there are significant changes in interpretation of "
"existing events or fields. Smaller changes, such as adding a new field to an "
"existing event, will not require an increment to the EVENT format version."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:350
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"version\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"evt\":\"4\",\t\t       # EVENT format version\n"
"\t\"exe\":\"2.20.1.155.g426c96fcdb\" # git version\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:352
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"too_many_files\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:356
msgid ""
"This event is written to the git-trace2-discard sentinel file if there are "
"too many files in the target trace directory (see the trace2.maxFiles config "
"option)."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:362
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"too_many_files\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:364
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"start\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:366
msgid "This event contains the complete argv received by main()."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:374
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"start\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"t_abs\":0.001227, # elapsed time in seconds\n"
"\t\"argv\":[\"git\",\"version\"]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:376
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"exit\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:378
msgid "This event is emitted when git calls `exit()`."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:386
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"exit\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"t_abs\":0.001227, # elapsed time in seconds\n"
"\t\"code\":0\t  # exit code\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:388
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"atexit\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:392
msgid ""
"This event is emitted by the Trace2 `atexit` routine during final shutdown.  "
"It should be the last event emitted by the process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:396
msgid ""
"(The elapsed time reported here is greater than the time reported in the "
"\"exit\" event because it runs after all other atexit tasks have completed.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:404
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"atexit\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"t_abs\":0.001227, # elapsed time in seconds\n"
"\t\"code\":0          # exit code\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:406
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"signal\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:410
msgid ""
"This event is emitted when the program is terminated by a user signal.  "
"Depending on the platform, the signal event may prevent the \"atexit\" event "
"from being generated."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:418
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"signal\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"t_abs\":0.001227,  # elapsed time in seconds\n"
"\t\"signo\":13         # SIGTERM, SIGINT, etc.\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:420
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"error\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:423
msgid ""
"This event is emitted when one of the `BUG()`, `bug()`, `error()`, `die()`, "
"`warning()`, or `usage()` functions are called."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:431
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"error\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"msg\":\"invalid option: --cahced\", # formatted error message\n"
"\t\"fmt\":\"invalid option: %s\"\t  # error format string\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:436
msgid ""
"The error event may be emitted more than once.  The format string allows "
"post-processors to group errors by type without worrying about specific "
"error arguments."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:437
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"cmd_path\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:440
msgid ""
"This event contains the discovered full path of the git executable (on "
"platforms that are configured to resolve it)."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:447
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"cmd_path\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"path\":\"C:/work/gfw/git.exe\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:449
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"cmd_ancestry\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:454
msgid ""
"This event contains the text command name for the parent (and earlier "
"generations of parents) of the current process, in an array ordered from "
"nearest parent to furthest great-grandparent. It may not be implemented on "
"all platforms."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:461
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"cmd_ancestry\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"ancestry\":[\"bash\",\"tmux: server\",\"systemd\"]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:463
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"cmd_name\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:466
msgid ""
"This event contains the command name for this git process and the hierarchy "
"of commands from parent git processes."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:474
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"cmd_name\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"name\":\"pack-objects\",\n"
"\t\"hierarchy\":\"push/pack-objects\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:479
msgid ""
"Normally, the \"name\" field contains the canonical name of the command.  "
"When a canonical name is not available, one of these special values are "
"used:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:486
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\"_query_\"            # \"git --html-path\"\n"
"\"_run_dashed_\"       # when \"git foo\" tries to run \"git-foo\"\n"
"\"_run_shell_alias_\"  # alias expansion to a shell command\n"
"\"_run_git_alias_\"    # alias expansion to a git command\n"
"\"_usage_\"            # usage error\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:488
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"cmd_mode\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:491
msgid ""
"This event, when present, describes the command variant. This event may be "
"emitted more than once."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:498
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"cmd_mode\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"name\":\"branch\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:504
msgid ""
"The \"name\" field is an arbitrary string to describe the command mode.  For "
"example, checkout can checkout a branch or an individual file.  And these "
"variations typically have different performance characteristics that are not "
"comparable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:505
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"alias\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:507
msgid "This event is present when an alias is expanded."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:515
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"alias\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"alias\":\"l\",\t\t # registered alias\n"
"\t\"argv\":[\"log\",\"--graph\"] # alias expansion\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:517
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"child_start\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:520
msgid "This event describes a child process that is about to be spawned."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:529
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"child_start\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"child_id\":2,\n"
"\t\"child_class\":\"?\",\n"
"\t\"use_shell\":false,\n"
"\t\"argv\":[\"git\",\"rev-list\",\"--objects\",\"--stdin\",\"--not\",\"--all\",\"--quiet\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:533
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t\"hook_name\":\"<hook_name>\"  # present when child_class is \"hook\"\n"
"\t\"cd\":\"<path>\"\t\t   # present when cd is required\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:537
msgid ""
"The \"child_id\" field can be used to match this child_start with the "
"corresponding child_exit event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:541
msgid ""
"The \"child_class\" field is a rough classification, such as \"editor\", "
"\"pager\", \"transport/*\", and \"hook\".  Unclassified children are "
"classified with \"?\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:542
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"child_exit\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:546
msgid ""
"This event is generated after the current process has returned from the "
"`waitpid()` and collected the exit information from the child."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:556
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"child_exit\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"child_id\":2,\n"
"\t\"pid\":14708,\t # child PID\n"
"\t\"code\":0,\t # child exit-code\n"
"\t\"t_rel\":0.110605 # observed run-time of child process\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:562
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:588
msgid ""
"Note that the session-id of the child process is not available to the "
"current/spawning process, so the child's PID is reported here as a hint for "
"post-processing.  (But it is only a hint because the child process may be a "
"shell script which doesn't have a session-id.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:568
msgid ""
"Note that the `t_rel` field contains the observed run time in seconds for "
"the child process (starting before the fork/exec/spawn and stopping after "
"the `waitpid()` and includes OS process creation overhead).  So this time "
"will be slightly larger than the atexit time reported by the child process "
"itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:569
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"child_ready\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:572
msgid ""
"This event is generated after the current process has started a background "
"process and released all handles to it."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:582
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"child_ready\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"child_id\":2,\n"
"\t\"pid\":14708,\t # child PID\n"
"\t\"ready\":\"ready\", # child ready state\n"
"\t\"t_rel\":0.110605 # observed run-time of child process\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:597
msgid ""
"This event is generated after the child is started in the background and "
"given a little time to boot up and start working.  If the child starts up "
"normally while the parent is still waiting, the \"ready\" field will have "
"the value \"ready\".  If the child is too slow to start and the parent times "
"out, the field will have the value \"timeout\".  If the child starts but the "
"parent is unable to probe it, the field will have the value \"error\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:602
msgid ""
"After the parent process emits this event, it will release all of its "
"handles to the child process and treat the child as a background daemon.  So "
"even if the child does eventually finish booting up, the parent will not "
"emit an updated event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:608
msgid ""
"Note that the `t_rel` field contains the observed run time in seconds when "
"the parent released the child process into the background.  The child is "
"assumed to be a long-running daemon process and may outlive the parent "
"process.  So the parent's child event times should not be compared to the "
"child's atexit times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:609
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"exec\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:612
msgid ""
"This event is generated before git attempts to `exec()` another command "
"rather than starting a child process."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:621
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"exec\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"exec_id\":0,\n"
"\t\"exe\":\"git\",\n"
"\t\"argv\":[\"foo\", \"bar\"]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:625
msgid ""
"The \"exec_id\" field is a command-unique id and is only useful if the "
"`exec()` fails and a corresponding exec_result event is generated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:626
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"exec_result\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:629
msgid ""
"This event is generated if the `exec()` fails and control returns to the "
"current git command."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:637
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"exec_result\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"exec_id\":0,\n"
"\t\"code\":1      # error code (errno) from exec()\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:639
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"thread_start\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:643
msgid ""
"This event is generated when a thread is started.  It is generated from "
"*within* the new thread's thread-proc (because it needs to access data in "
"the thread's thread-local storage)."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:650
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"thread_start\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"thread\":\"th02:preload_thread\" # thread name\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:652
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"thread_exit\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:655
msgid ""
"This event is generated when a thread exits.  It is generated from *within* "
"the thread's thread-proc."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:663
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"thread_exit\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"thread\":\"th02:preload_thread\", # thread name\n"
"\t\"t_rel\":0.007328                # thread elapsed time\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:665
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"def_param\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:668
msgid ""
"This event is generated to log a global parameter, such as a config setting, "
"command-line flag, or environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:677
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"def_param\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"scope\":\"global\",\n"
"\t\"param\":\"core.abbrev\",\n"
"\t\"value\":\"7\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:679
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"def_repo\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:682
msgid ""
"This event defines a repo-id and associates it with the root of the "
"worktree."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:690
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"def_repo\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"repo\":1,\n"
"\t\"worktree\":\"/Users/jeffhost/work/gfw\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:696
msgid ""
"As stated earlier, the repo-id is currently always 1, so there will only be "
"one def_repo event.  Later, if in-proc submodules are supported, a def_repo "
"event should be emitted for each submodule visited."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:697
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"region_enter\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:699
msgid "This event is generated when entering a region."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:710
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"region_enter\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"repo\":1,                # optional\n"
"\t\"nesting\":1,             # current region stack depth\n"
"\t\"category\":\"index\",      # optional\n"
"\t\"label\":\"do_read_index\", # optional\n"
"\t\"msg\":\".git/index\"       # optional\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:714
msgid ""
"The `category` field may be used in a future enhancement to do "
"category-based filtering."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:717
msgid ""
"`GIT_TRACE2_EVENT_NESTING` or `trace2.eventNesting` can be used to filter "
"deeply nested regions and data events.  It defaults to \"2\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:718
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"region_leave\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:720
msgid "This event is generated when leaving a region."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:732
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"region_leave\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"repo\":1,                # optional\n"
"\t\"t_rel\":0.002876,        # time spent in region in seconds\n"
"\t\"nesting\":1,             # region stack depth\n"
"\t\"category\":\"index\",      # optional\n"
"\t\"label\":\"do_read_index\", # optional\n"
"\t\"msg\":\".git/index\"       # optional\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:734
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"data\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:737
msgid "This event is generated to log a thread- and region-local key/value pair."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:750
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"data\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"repo\":1,              # optional\n"
"\t\"t_abs\":0.024107,      # absolute elapsed time\n"
"\t\"t_rel\":0.001031,      # elapsed time in region/thread\n"
"\t\"nesting\":2,           # region stack depth\n"
"\t\"category\":\"index\",\n"
"\t\"key\":\"read/cache_nr\",\n"
"\t\"value\":\"3552\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:753
msgid "The \"value\" field may be an integer or a string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:754
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"data-json\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:757
msgid ""
"This event is generated to log a pre-formatted JSON string containing "
"structured data."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:770
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"data_json\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"repo\":1,              # optional\n"
"\t\"t_abs\":0.015905,\n"
"\t\"t_rel\":0.015905,\n"
"\t\"nesting\":1,\n"
"\t\"category\":\"process\",\n"
"\t\"key\":\"windows/ancestry\",\n"
"\t\"value\":[\"bash.exe\",\"bash.exe\"]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:772
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"th_timer\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:776
msgid ""
"This event logs the amount of time that a stopwatch timer was running in the "
"thread.  This event is generated when a thread exits for timers that "
"requested per-thread events."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:788
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"th_timer\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"category\":\"my_category\",\n"
"\t\"name\":\"my_timer\",\n"
"\t\"intervals\":5,         # number of time it was started/stopped\n"
"\t\"t_total\":0.052741,    # total time in seconds it was running\n"
"\t\"t_min\":0.010061,      # shortest interval\n"
"\t\"t_max\":0.011648       # longest interval\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:790
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"timer\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:794
msgid ""
"This event logs the amount of time that a stopwatch timer was running "
"aggregated across all threads.  This event is generated when the process "
"exits."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:806
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"timer\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"category\":\"my_category\",\n"
"\t\"name\":\"my_timer\",\n"
"\t\"intervals\":5,         # number of time it was started/stopped\n"
"\t\"t_total\":0.052741,    # total time in seconds it was running\n"
"\t\"t_min\":0.010061,      # shortest interval\n"
"\t\"t_max\":0.011648       # longest interval\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:808
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"th_counter\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:812
msgid ""
"This event logs the value of a counter variable in a thread.  This event is "
"generated when a thread exits for counters that requested per-thread events."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:821
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"th_counter\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"category\":\"my_category\",\n"
"\t\"name\":\"my_counter\",\n"
"\t\"count\":23\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:823
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"counter\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:827
msgid ""
"This event logs the value of a counter variable across all threads.  This "
"event is generated when the process exits.  The total value reported here is "
"the sum across all threads."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:836
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"counter\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"category\":\"my_category\",\n"
"\t\"name\":\"my_counter\",\n"
"\t\"count\":23\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:838
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"printf\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:841
msgid ""
"This event logs a human-readable message with no particular formatting "
"guidelines."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:849
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"\t\"event\":\"printf\",\n"
"\t...\n"
"\t\"t_abs\":0.015905,      # elapsed time in seconds\n"
"\t\"msg\":\"Hello world\"    # optional\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:852
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example Trace2 API Usage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:856
msgid ""
"Here is a hypothetical usage of the Trace2 API showing the intended usage "
"(without worrying about the actual Git details)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:857
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:861
msgid ""
"Initialization happens in `main()`.  Behind the scenes, an `atexit` and "
"`signal` handler are registered."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:866
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int main(int argc, const char **argv)\n"
"{\n"
"\tint exit_code;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:869
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\ttrace2_initialize();\n"
"\ttrace2_cmd_start(argv);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:871
#, no-wrap
msgid "\texit_code = cmd_main(argc, argv);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:873
#, no-wrap
msgid "\ttrace2_cmd_exit(exit_code);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:876
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\treturn exit_code;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:878
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command Details"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:882
msgid ""
"After the basics are established, additional command information can be sent "
"to Trace2 as it is discovered."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:889
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"int cmd_checkout(int argc, const char **argv)\n"
"{\n"
"\ttrace2_cmd_name(\"checkout\");\n"
"\ttrace2_cmd_mode(\"branch\");\n"
"\ttrace2_def_repo(the_repository);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:892
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t// emit \"def_param\" messages for \"interesting\" config settings.\n"
"\ttrace2_cmd_list_config();\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:895
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tif (do_something())\n"
"\t    trace2_cmd_error(\"Path '%s': cannot do something\", path);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:898
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:1316
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\treturn 0;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:900
#, no-wrap
msgid "Child Processes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:903
msgid "Wrap code spawning child processes."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:911
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"void run_child(...)\n"
"{\n"
"\tint child_exit_code;\n"
"\tstruct child_process cmd = CHILD_PROCESS_INIT;\n"
"\t...\n"
"\tcmd.trace2_child_class = \"editor\";\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:916
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\ttrace2_child_start(&cmd);\n"
"\tchild_exit_code = spawn_child_and_wait_for_it();\n"
"\ttrace2_child_exit(&cmd, child_exit_code);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:921
msgid ""
"For example, the following fetch command spawned ssh, index-pack, rev-list, "
"and gc.  This example also shows that fetch took 5.199 seconds and of that "
"4.932 was in ssh."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:927
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:963
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ export GIT_TRACE2_BRIEF=1\n"
"$ export GIT_TRACE2=~/log.normal\n"
"$ git fetch origin\n"
"...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:948
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cat ~/log.normal\n"
"version 2.20.1.vfs.1.1.47.g534dbe1ad1\n"
"start git fetch origin\n"
"worktree /Users/jeffhost/work/gfw\n"
"cmd_name fetch (fetch)\n"
"child_start[0] ssh git@github.com ...\n"
"child_start[1] git index-pack ...\n"
"... (Trace2 events from child processes omitted)\n"
"child_exit[1] pid:14707 code:0 elapsed:0.076353\n"
"child_exit[0] pid:14706 code:0 elapsed:4.931869\n"
"child_start[2] git rev-list ...\n"
"... (Trace2 events from child process omitted)\n"
"child_exit[2] pid:14708 code:0 elapsed:0.110605\n"
"child_start[3] git gc --auto\n"
"... (Trace2 events from child process omitted)\n"
"child_exit[3] pid:14709 code:0 elapsed:0.006240\n"
"exit elapsed:5.198503 code:0\n"
"atexit elapsed:5.198541 code:0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:957
msgid ""
"When a git process is a (direct or indirect) child of another git process, "
"it inherits Trace2 context information.  This allows the child to print the "
"command hierarchy.  This example shows gc as child[3] of fetch.  When the gc "
"process reports its name as \"gc\", it also reports the hierarchy as "
"\"fetch/gc\".  (In this example, trace2 messages from the child process is "
"indented for clarity.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/api-trace2.txt:982
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cat ~/log.normal\n"
"version 2.20.1.160.g5676107ecd.dirty\n"
"start git fetch official\n"
"worktree /Users/jeffhost/work/gfw\n"
"cmd_name fetch (fetch)\n"
"...\n"
"child_start[3] git gc --auto\n"
"    version 2.20.1.160.g5676107ecd.dirty\n"
"    start /Users/jeffhost/work/gfw/git gc --auto\n"
"    worktree /Users/jeffhost/work/gfw\n"
"    cmd_name gc (fetch/gc)\n"
"    exit elapsed:0.001959 code:0\n"
"    atexit elapsed:0.001997 code:0\n"
"child_exit[3] pid:20303 code:0 elapsed:0.007564\n"
"exit elapsed:3.868938 code:0\n"
"atexit elapsed:3.868970 code:0\n"
msgstr ""

